Why do most crypto traders fail?

There are many reasons for this, but I will name the most basic and, in my opinion, the most common reasons for failure in crypto:

- Inability to properly analyze the market and trading with an unprofitable trading strategy. This turns trading into a game of chance, with a correspondingly negative outcome;

- Deliberately violating risk management in order to make a big profit quickly. With this approach, just one or a few unsuccessful trades with an inflated lot size can wipe out an entire deposit;

- Inability to control one's emotions and lack of discipline, which leads to impulsive and unsystematic decisions contrary to the rules and conditions of one's strategy, which, even with a good strategy, will still result in unprofitable trading;

- Unwillingness to constantly learn and improve, which leads to stagnation in trading and a complete lack of improvement;

- a constant desire to quickly recoup losses after losing trades and immediately take revenge on the market, as well as a desire to constantly be in the market, which leads to overtrading and, consequently, fatigue, frequent mistakes, and losses.
